{
"cls": "svc",
"inst": 3,
"brief": "Service 'B': online retail service, 28 sessions per second, 53% of users on mobile (RTT 65 ms) and the rest on desktop; application pool of 10 workers; database with 3 workers; base conversion 2.6% mobile / 4.8% desktop; profit margin 19%; p95 page-time SLO 2.5 s.\nOptional capabilities (flag: what it does; its main costs and risks):\n- CDN: Edge content delivery network (edge caching of static content, shorter round trips; page weight x1.05; fixed cost 255/h; operational complexity 1.0)\n- COMP: Response compression (+3.5 ms CPU per page; page weight x0.61; operational complexity 0.3)\n- CACHE: Application data cache (+0.5 ms CPU per page; database calls x0.35; page weight x1.06; fixed cost 90/h; operational complexity 0.8)\n- REPL: Three extra application replicas (page weight x0.97; +3 application workers; fixed cost 1114/h; operational complexity 0.6)\n- RECO: ML recommendation service (+17 ms ML inference per page; page weight x1.07; +0.4 pages per session; fixed cost 2080/h; operational complexity 1.7)\n- CHAT: Generative-AI shopping assistant (+2.0 ms CPU per page; page weight x0.95; +45 ms external API delay per page; 0.069 per session; operational complexity 1.7)\n- ONECLICK: One-click checkout (page weight x1.05; -1.0 pages per session; fraud losses x1.25; operational complexity 0.6)\n- MFA: Step-up authentication (+1.7 ms CPU per page; page weight x0.78; 0.019 per session; fraud losses x0.25; operational complexity 0.8)\n- MEDIA: Rich product media (page weight x2.41; fixed cost 227/h; operational complexity 0.4)\n- AUTOC: Search autocomplete (+2.4 ms CPU per page; page weight x1.20; -0.3 pages per session; operational complexity 0.6)\n- PRIV: Privacy dashboard and consent manager (page weight x1.09; fixed cost 70/h; operational complexity 0.6)\n- TELEM: Fine-grained behavioural telemetry (+2.3 ms CPU per page; page weight x0.98; fixed cost 696/h; operational complexity 0.9)\nKnown interactions: recommendations work much better with behavioural telemetry; step-up authentication largely cancels the gain of one-click checkout; a privacy dashboard offsets the friction of authentication and telemetry; the assistant can use recommendations; rich media and the assistant compete for attention.\nA configuration is judged by a weighted utility: user conversion (weight 0.45), feasibility (0.25: p95 latency within the SLO, no overload, low complexity) and hourly profit after infrastructure, bandwidth, per-session and fraud costs (0.30). Overloading the application pool (utilisation above ~95%) is catastrophic for latency and conversion.",
